10:T1778,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Recipe","mainEntityOfPage":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes/","name":"Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes","image":["https://crave.devyy.com/ai-images/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes.jpg","https://crave.devyy.com/ai-images/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes.jpg"],"datePublished":"2026-11-01","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"@crave_testkitchen"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Crave Recipes","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/icon-512.png","width":512,"height":512}},"description":"Global-inspired handesh – bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes with 6 measured ingredients — zero sign-up, instant Cook Mode. Ready in 45 mins (6 servings). 4.9★ rated with US/Metric scaling & hands-free Cook Mode.","prepTime":"PT15M","cookTime":"PT30M","totalTime":"PT45M","recipeYield":"6 servings","recipeCategory":"Cakes & Mug Cakes","recipeCuisine":"Global","keywords":"Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes, Global, Cakes & Mug Cakes, #Handesh, #CraveMadeMeDoIt, #ViralDesserts, #GlobalSweets","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"420 calories"},"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":4.9,"reviewCount":68},"recipeIngredient":["1.11 cup Date Molasses","1.67 cup Warm Water","1.11 cup Rice Flour","10 tbsp Flour","0.25 tsp Ground Cinnamon","0.25 tsp Ground Cardomom"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Whisk & Combine Base Ingredients","text":"Add the molasses to a large mixing bowl and begin by pouring 300ml of water to start with and whisk together. The texture of Bangladeshi molasses varies from a thick syrup to slightly set. I use brands such as Zilani or Akza. If the set is very syrupy (like golden syrup) you will only require 300–325ml of water Pour in the flours and spices (if using) and whisk for 3–5 minutes, until you have a smooth batter. You need to check carefully for lumps, as they prevent the handesh from rising and will cause them to split. Cover the batter and rest for 2 hours. Incorporate 1.11 cup date molasses, 1.67 cup warm water, 1.11 cup rice flour, and 10 tbsp flour smoothly until evenly distributed.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes/#step-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Fry Until Golden & Crisp","text":"After 2 hours, thoroughly whisk the batter until smooth, as the rice flour will have settled at the bottom of the bowl. The batter should have a fairly thick consistency, yet remain loose enough to pour – similar to thick pancake or waffle batter. It should form ribbons as you drag the whisk though it Take a cast-iron korai or wok and add enough oil to half-fill the pan, or enough to deep-fry and turn the heat to high. Once the oil is hot reduce the heat to low–medium. Drop in a teaspoon of batter to test the oil – if it rises slowly to the surface the oil is ready. Incorporate 0.25 tsp ground cinnamon and 0.25 tsp ground cardomom smoothly until evenly distributed.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes/#step-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Fry Until Golden & Crisp","text":"Pour batter in a quick steady stream into the centre of the pan, preferably using a pyrex jug with a pouring spout (About 45ml of batter for each cake). It should rise to the surface in about 15–20 seconds and slowly puff up. If it rises too quickly, just turn the heat down slightly. Cook for 45 seconds, or until the underside is golden. Carefully turn over and cook for a further 30–45 seconds, until golden. Make sure to not let excess batter drip into the pan as this may prevent the cakes from rising and always fry one at a time If the batter splits while frying, whisk in 2 tablespoons of flour to the mixture and try again. You should be creating handesh which are about the size of a digestive biscuit.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes/#step-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Drain Crisp, Garnish & Serve Warm","text":"Use a slotted spoon to remove the handesh and place on kitchen towel with frilled edge facing down while you continue frying the reaming batter. This helps retain the shape of the cakes Enjoy hot, fresh out of the pan. Once cool, place in an airtight container overnight and in the fridge for up to a week. Reheat in a warm oven for a few minutes to refresh or on a tawa or frying pan over a very low heat, turning a few times.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes/#step-4"}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Cakes & Mug Cakes","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/category/cakes-cupcakes/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/handesh-bangladeshi-rice-flour-and-date-molasses-cakes/"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to make Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes takes 45 minutes total (15 minutes prep) and yields 6 servings at 420 calories per serving."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I make Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes healthier or with zero refined sugar?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes! Toggle the Healthy Swap mode on this Handesh – Bangladeshi rice flour and date molasses cakes recipe page to convert ingredients into lower-sugar, higher-protein, or wholesome alternatives automatically."}}]}]}5:[["$","script",null,{"id":"crave-recipe-jsonld","type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$10"}}],"$L11","$L12"]
